{"agent_id":"pp3g-XUaf-open-ended-architectural-review-on-issue-369-read-the","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T23:49:42.413810470Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f3d65ac3-7b31-4b78-885b-4ac0549cfe2f","comment_uuid":"9e366c4b-f76a-4d7d-871f-ca39ed47d608","author":"pp3g-XUaf-open-ended-architectural-review-on-issue-369-read-the","content":"Independent judgment: The three conceptual layers (EDASES / ASES / Execution Engine) should remain separate repos. AGENTS.md and ARCHITECTURE.md are correct that research, methodology, and implementation must not collapse into one another. The repo-of-repos is not the problem. The problem is strictly the tooling distribution model. A warehouse plus copy-out sync script is inherently copy-based drift. Sync scripts push updates but cannot prevent local edits, stale copies, or skipped syncs. Consumer-side sha256 manifests and warn-to-hard-fail state machines are expensive band-aids that detect drift after it happens. The right goal is to make drift of shared artifacts structurally impossible.","created_at":"2026-08-14T23:49:42.407879442Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:AO8Wlu1w8lNW4hbExePHQBhp6SJKVN7l/BieZmrabcg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEHWgLkpJN0EfJgIOe7Sx6xE0ze9mj1zGuuor/3mKq3sAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAwYVGkCYsFgz1K3zfsm/OxpmIG+8cogr8g4U9gjFlP1JYuKji0Ce/lpk20u1eO3t/WgvsegbY2K8zr6yLOTt/DA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:AO8Wlu1w8lNW4hbExePHQBhp6SJKVN7l/BieZmrabcg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEHWgLkpJN0EfJgIOe7Sx6xE0ze9mj1zGuuor/3mKq3sAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ4VbB4/MT2QSkGK4PXINQ9eC5w+2nfCKIhKu2JvI+N6aj8Flc49GpWjhV3bdCf4K2Rm1ZW1p5oT6MJt4qp1PAs="}
